Well, thanks for this bit of wisdom.  You've astounded me.  Anyway,
you'd better come tell my VMS box all this, because it's running Motif
just fine.

The demos that come with Motif under VMS, in
sys$common:[decw$motif.demos], are *exact* duplicates of the demos that
come with Motif for Ultrix, in /usr/lib/DXM/demos.  By *exact*, I mean
line for line.  And they compile and run under both platforms just fine.

If you write your programs correctly, there will be no problems.
Remember that VAX-C isn't ANSI compliant, but neither is cc.  You need
to write your code for cc if you want the widest audience.

Anyway, the point is, correctly written code doesn't have to be "ported"
to VMS, just ftp'd and recompiled.  The same code should work under VMS,
Ultrix, and HP-UX without changes.  The Motif demos do...

