I have been following these threads with GREAT interest and after
reflecting on our situation I think I know what bugs me/our company the
most.

We use VAX/Ultrix as our product base using the Ingres RDBMS.  Primarily
have been selling MicroVax 3xxx systems.  I have few complaints about
ULTRIX - could be MUCH better documented - could REALLY use shared
libraries.  Overall it is VERY reliable - I can not recollect a single OS
panic on a customer machine related to software bugs - with one BUT
LAT support (several cans of worms here). The hardware we use (VAX 3100/20e)
is price competitive with adequeate - for our needs - performance.

I have been observing the following:

Mid 1991 - hmm... new Vax (E.g. 4000/xxx) anouncments don't support
Ultrix - talk to sales rep - Well MIPS is our Ultrix platform but won't
drop VAX support.

October 30, 1991 Customer Update - page 65:
    A future relase of the ULTRIX operating system will provide support
    for all new and previously announced VAX 4000 and MicroVAX 3100
    systems.  Availability is currently planned for the second half of
    1992.
Ok.  We can live with that - just wait and all will be well.

Dec 1991 - DEC announces MicroVAX 3100 models 30,40 and 80 AND drops
the MicroVAX 3100 20e (our most cost effective - well only cost effective
BOX)!!!!  We are shocked.  Talk to Sales rep - well still can order ...
Ultrix coming .... OK will wait.

Feb 1992 - Call up Ingres and ask for latest release (6.4 - which of course
fixes all our problems :-)  Get polite answer that 6.4 will NEVER be
available for Ultrix - only on OSF/1 on Vaxen - REASON: DEC direction.
Now I start to get concerned.  Call in Sales Rep - express forcefully our
concerns - Answer: sorry dropped that  ball on you HOWEVER OSF/1 coming
soon - First on MIPS/Alpha then VAXen.

May 1992 - Hear via the net - NO OSF/1 A POSSIBILITY FOR MIPS/VAX boxes.

SUMMARY:

DEC:  You have been changing your story too often in the past year for
anyone to take ANY story you tell us as THE PLAN.  We (i.e. your customers)
can not plan our future BECAUSE:

1. The future changes all the time
2. You don't work HARD at informing your existing base on changes which
   affect them.

I/We can live with changes and changing a boxes status to maintenance
etc.  JUST KEEP US INFORMED and DON'T CHANGE THE STORY EVERY 2-3 MONTHS!!
