This isn't in response to any particular note, but it does seem to fit
this thread.

There are a lot of people in DEC who believe that there is no money to
be made on operating system software; worse, they believe that it is
a money losing proposition.  Further, when you take into account the
margins needed to sell hardware, you can no longer have hardware revenue
to subsidize the hardware.

I think that one could make a good case for there being more people doing
development work on all the unix o/s software industry wide than there
are doing development work on all the CPU boxes industry wide.

I suspect that a lot of people in the industry see o/s development as
