such like. I can't understand why any company would want to put so
much enery into developing two (or more?) major operating systems in
parallel for the next 10 years or so when they are converging to a
functionally common point.  I would understand it if the systems were
totally different and were used in different environments.  However,
that's not the case with VMS and OSF/1.  They look and feel the same
to an x-windows user and they offer almost the same features to the
program developer, particulary when both become fully POSIX compliant.
Digital may boast about these achievements but I feel it's a luxury
they can't afford. This dual approach can only weaken the quality of
what they can offer in competition from other companies unless Digital
has found a way to clone multi-tasking people in their labs.

