> 
>I want to know how to set a background job back to 
>foreground job after I have logout my terminal.

    I don't think it's possible.  When you logout, and outstanding children
    your process had in the background are bumped up the tree to become direct
    descendents of the init process.  As far as I know (which is pretty
    limited in this area), there is no way to take a child away from init and
    graft it onto a new parent.

