One subtle problem which took us a few weeks to track down is that
the National Instruments driver has LUN 3 hard-coded into it (well,
maybe it's their subroutine library, not the driver - It's been a
while since we played with it).  If your program assigns LUN 3 to
something, you will get flaky behavior.

We finally ended up scrapping the PDP system and getting a SCSI/HPIB
adapter from NI to hook up to our VAXstation 3100.  This ended up
working much more easily and reliably (so far).  Now if there were
just a _good_ Tek 4010/4014 emulator for VMS/DECwindows....




