In article <Bonq3u.D5p@news.cso.uiuc.edu> e-sink@uiuc.edu writes:
>Anyone know how we can iconify and deiconify windows under dxwm
>from our code ??

Dxwm is not ICCCM-compliant since it sort of pre-dates the ICCCM.  I
believe that something like the following code, from an old version of
xrooms written at DEC, should work:

	event.xclient.type = ClientMessage;
	event.xclient.display = dpy;
	event.xclient.window = client;
	event.xclient.message_type = WM_CHANGE_STATE;
	event.xclient.format = 32;
	event.xclient.data.l[0] = IconicState;
	XSendEvent(dpy, RootWindowOfScreen(scrn), False,
		   SubstructureRedirectMask | SubstructureNotifyMask,
		   &event);

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
