|> are my own, and don't reflect DEC's.

I didn't "complain vigorously" to my Rep, but I did call and ask some
questions.

This is the _current_ plan...

OSF/1 will be supported on the Mips R3000 platforms (i.e., DECstation
5000's, etc).  OSF/1 is not supported on the R2000 boxes (DS3100, etc).

There is discussion on whether it will be ported to the R4000 line of
machines.  Currently it is not.  DEC is waiting to see the demand for
OSF/1 on the R3000 platforms.  If it is reasonable enough, they will
port it to the R4000 boxes.

This is different from what was anticipated or interpreted many months
ago (such as the lack of the R2000 platforms being supported and question
on whether the R4000's will be supported), but a decision to not support
OSF/1 on the Mips line as reported by the "trade rags" is not accurate.

If OSF/1 is important on your R4000 machines, it would seem to make
sense to indicate that to your representative(s).  Support on the 
R2000's seems unlikely at any cost since those machines are effectively
discontinued.

