When I was doing testing of DECnsr support for RS/6000 clients, I
regularly backed up all the filesystems on an RS/6000 in Nashua, N.H.
to my server here near Seattle.  No fancy extended LAN was needed.
Just TCP/IP connectivity.  Of course it DID take longer than a backup
of one of the systems on my local ethernet :-)

I too feel safer with a full backup once in a while.  However, a
couple of days ago, I blew the entire /usr partition on my workstation
(don't ask how!).  Using DECnsr, I was able to recover the whole thing
myself in a pretty short period of time (with a polite mail message to
our operators to have the necessary tapes standing by).  This based on
a schedule of monthly backups, with various level backups on a daily
basis.

Oh.  DECnsr will soon backup PCs too.


