	IBM released a version of AIX with TCF (Transparent Computing
Facility) for PS/2 and System 370 machines about 2? years ago.  It allowed
processes to migrate between machines with like architectures.  Processes
were not automatically migrated, but could either migrate themselves or be
moved by user commands.  I stopped working on AIX systems about that time so
I don't know how much farther they took this technology, but they did in fact
have process migration in a commercial UNIX product at that time.
Unfortunately, they used a completely different kernel base on the RS/6000
line and to the best of my knowledge this functionality has not yet been put
into AIX for the RS/6000s.  Much of the technology involved was from Locus.

