Does anyone have a C (or Fortran) source module for DEC Fortran/RISC
which provides the VMS STR$TRIM function?  I've had a go at writing
it in C but as yet it doesn't work:

VMS definition is STR$TRIM(dst, src [, len])

int str_trim_(char *s1, char *s2, long *l, long l1, long l2)
{
        int             i;
        int             l0;

        *l = 0;
        l0 = (l1 < l2) ? l1 : l2;
        for (i = 0; i < l0; ++i) {
                if (*s2 != ' ' && *s2 != '\t') {
                        *l = i + 1;
                }
                *s1++ = *s2++;
        }
}

