In article <1992May15.151450.16061@linus.mitre.org>, cazier@mbunix.mitre.org (Cazier) writes:
> 
> One question is why is Ultrix not clusterable? Will OSF/1 correct this?

It depends on what you expect by "clusterable".  ULTRIX supports HSC
today, though the only system with a CI adapter is the DECsystem
5800.  I've heard of people building dual host configurations using
the DSSI adapters of the DECsystem 5500.  System to system failover
of disks is possible, but is complicated by the lack of a good way
to really determine "the other" system is truly dead and the presence
of Prestoserve.  Within system failover could probably be done as a 
intermediate device driver.

The hardest problem to solve is presented by the shared file system
of VAXclusters.  VMS has the benefit of the lock manager to handle
VAXcluster wide locks needed by the file system code to make sure
everybody updates everything in the right order.  Even if ULTRIX
had the lock manager, trying to keep the buffer caches of all the
participating systems the same in the face of writes make it a very
hard problem.

This just assumes you're happy with non-mixed clusters.  Getting
ULTRIX and VMS to be able to read and share each others file systems
and have each provide all the required VAXcluster services would
seem to be an even harder problem.
-- 
Alan Rollow				alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com



