To ...ummm... clarify slightly, the standard C compilers shipped with OSF/MIPS
and ULTRIX/MIPS use different front ends.  The ULTRIX/MIPS version is pcc-based
with some ANSI extensions (e.g., partial prototype support) known as 'ccom';
the OSF/MIPS version is a rewritten ANSI-compliant version (known as 'cfe'). 
While cfe will accept most programs written for K&R, there are sometimes subtle
differences.

There is an ANSI-compliant C compiler available on ULTRIX/MIPS called 'c89'; I
believe it is also available for OSF/MIPS, but if it matters, you should contact
your Digital representative to be sure.  It's not the default compiler, in any
case.

Credentials: I was part of the compiler engineering team for those releases.
