Hi there,

I'm an infrequent UNIX user and I always (automaticly) try to use the EDT
keypad in vi. Which doesn't lead to correct results :-)

I customized an .exrc file with some map commands. Does someone have a more
sophisticated .exrc for a poor and stupid VMS user like me? :-)

I'm aware of EMACS EDT emulation, but on several machines I only have vi
and no space to install EMACS.
Please no flames on "why EDT?  vi is the best editor of the world!" etc
etc..

Here my .exrc so far:

map ^[[2~ "aP
map ^[[3~ "ad`a
map ^[Ov "ad`a
map ^[[4~ ma
map ^[[5~ kkkkkkkkkkk
map ^[[6~ jjjjjjjjjjj
map ^[OP P
map ^[OS "ld$
map ^[OS d$
map ^[Om "wdw
map ^[Om dw
map ^[Ol "cdl
map ^[Ol x
map ^[Op ^M
map ^[Oq w
map ^[Or $
map ^[On ma
map ^? X
map ^[[A k
map ^[[B j
map ^[[C l
map ^[[D h
map ^[[23~ ^[
map! ^[[23~ ^[

PS: I use a VT220

