Thats TZ85. I have been using that for the last 3 months and I can vouch for
its reliability. It is also MUCH faster than the Exabyte drives. It can pull
up [on a DECStation 5000/240] data from the disk as fast as the disk can
supply it. And on the 240, we are talking about files from a RZ58 to TZ85
on the same DMA SCSI. Now thats fast! I can see 3x improvement over 8mm.

Reha Elci
Email: elci@bugs.gs.com

PS: eprom updates are provided on a tape which the drive uploads itself
with no intervention from the CPU. way cool.



